    {"id":"BMCI-09","name":"New Tilak Bridge (twin cable-stayed ROB), Dadar","shortName":"Tilak bridge","summary":"A six-lane, 600 m twin cable-stayed bridge being built by the BMC and MahaRail next to the century-old Tilak Bridge in Dadar. In June 2026 it was about 70% done; the first three-lane arm is expected by April 2027 and full completion by 2028.","sector":"Roads & bridges","agency":"MRIDC","status":"In progress","progress":70,"cost":{"original":375,"revised":null},"funders":[{"name":"BMC","type":"Municipal","amount":null,"note":"Joint BMC–MRIDC project; funding split not stated in sources"}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":"2028","revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["Dadar East","Dadar West"],"constituencies":["Mahim","Wadala"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://thechenabtimes.com/2026/06/19/mumbais-dadar-set-for-traffic-relief-with-new-cable-stayed-tilak-bridge/?amp=1","title":"The Chenab Times","date":"2026-06-19","claim":"Rs 375 crore, 600 m, six lanes; BMC with MRIDC; phase 1 target April 2026, full completion 2028"},{"url":"https://swarajyamag.com/amp/story/news-brief/mumbais-new-six-lane-cable-stayed-tilak-bridge-to-open-in-phases-from-2027-report","title":"Swarajya","date":null,"claim":"About 70% complete; to open in phases from early 2027"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.019,"lng":72.842},"evidence":"single","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"BMCI-10","name":"Mogra storm-water pumping station, Andheri West","shortName":"Mogra pumping station","summary":"One of the eight pumping stations recommended after the 2005 floods, on the Mogra nullah near Lokhandwala, to cut flooding in Versova, Andheri and Jogeshwari. After two decades of land, litigation and coastal-clearance hurdles, the BMC said construction would start on 15 October 2026, with commissioning aimed before 2029.","sector":"Flood control","agency":"BMC","status":"Delayed","progress":0,"cost":{"original":393,"revised":null,"note":"Rs 393 crore sanctioned in 2021; part of the Rs 13,000-crore integrated flood control plan"},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":"2029","completedDate":null,"delayReason":"Land acquisition, litigation (court allowed work in Dec 2024 subject to a Rs 33 crore deposit), a site clash with Versova–Dahisar Coastal Road Phase 2, and the site shift needing fresh CRZ and MoEFCC clearances","areas":["Andheri West","Lokhandwala","Oshiwara","Versova","Jogeshwari"],"constituencies":["Versova","Andheri West"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mogra-pumping-station-work-to-begin-on-october-15-after-20-year-wait-to-ease-andheri-flooding","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-10-04","claim":"Work to begin 15 Oct 2026 after clearances; Rs 393 crore; aim to commission before 2029; delay reasons"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-flood-mitigation-bmcs-mogra-pumping-station-project-moves-closer-to-reality-after-czma-clearance","title":"Free Press Journal","date":null,"claim":"MCZMA clearance received (2026)"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.142,"lng":72.821},"statusUnchecked":true,"evidence":"single","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"BMCI-11","name":"Mahul storm-water pumping station, Wadala","shortName":"Mahul pumping station","summary":"A post-2005-flood pumping station on salt-pan land at Wadala, meant to cut waterlogging in Sion, Matunga, Kurla and Chembur. The contractor was chosen in 2018, but land handover from the Salt Commissioner has dragged on, and the cost rose to about Rs 605 crore in October 2025. Construction had not been reported as started.","sector":"Flood control","agency":"BMC","status":"Stalled","progress":0,"cost":{"original":403,"revised":605.28,"note":"Contractor's 2018 quote was Rs 462 crore; revision covers updated rates, 7-year maintenance and extra pumps"},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":"Laxmi-Avighna-Villo (JV)","startDate":null,"targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":"Acquiring 6.17 acres of salt-pan land controlled by the Salt Commissioner and used by Hormuz Salt Works; environmental (MoEF) clearances","areas":["Wadala","Sion","Matunga","Kurla","Chembur"],"constituencies":["Sion Koliwada"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-flood-mitigation-mahul-pumping-station-cost-escalates-to-605-crore-due-to-land-acquisition-delays","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-10-17","claim":"Cost up from Rs 403 crore to Rs 605.28 crore; contractor Laxmi-Avighna-Villo JV; 6.17 acres at Wadala still being acquired"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-bmcs-mogra-mahul-pumping-stations-face-delays-over-land-acquisition-moef-clearances","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-03","claim":"Salt-pan land still not secured; MoEF clearances pending"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.029,"lng":72.874},"evidence":"single","statusUnchecked":true,"recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"BMCI-12","name":"Manori desalination plant (200 MLD, expandable to 400 MLD)","shortName":"Manori desalination plant","summary":"Mumbai's first sea-water desalination plant, 200 MLD expandable to 400 MLD, on a 12-hectare plot at Manori. The tender floated in December 2023 failed four times before bids came in. The BMC signed a letter of acceptance with GVPR Engineers in December 2025 for a total of Rs 11,166.17 crore, which includes 20 years of operation. IDE Technologies supplies the reverse-osmosis technology. The project received CRZ clearance in April 2026. In July 2026 the BMC said all permissions were in place and full work on the ground would start after the monsoon. No report confirms that construction has begun. The first 200 MLD phase is targeted for 2029.","sector":"Water & sanitation","agency":"BMC","status":"Not started","progress":null,"cost":{"original":null,"revised":11166.17,"note":"Rs 11,166.17 crore total contract value (Dec 2025), including Rs 4,077 crore construction, Rs 2,067 crore 20-year O&M, Rs 3,646.57 crore electricity, plus 18% GST and contingencies. In Oct 2025 the estimate was raised to Rs 3,500 crore from an initial tender estimate of Rs 2,000 crore (FPJ); ThePrint (Jul 2026) put the first phase at about Rs 3,900 crore."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":"GVPR Engineers Ltd (civil works); IDE Technologies (reverse-osmosis technology and 20-year operation)","startDate":null,"targetDate":"2029","revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":"Tender floated December 2023 failed four times before bids were received","areas":["Manori","Gorai","Malad West"],"constituencies":["Malad West"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-bmc-finalises-11166-crore-manori-desalination-plant-deal-with-gvpr-engineers-after-bid-cut-of-494-cr","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-12-05","claim":"LoA with GVPR Engineers; Rs 11,166.17 crore total; 200 MLD expandable to 400; construction to start 2026"},{"url":"https://theprint.in/ground-reports/mumbai-is-running-out-of-drinking-water-a-desalination-plant-in-manori-is-bmcs-solution/2998517/","title":"ThePrint","date":"2026-07-28","claim":"Final CRZ clearance 28 Apr 2026; BMC says all permissions received and full ground work to start post-monsoon; first phase about Rs 3,900 crore, 200 MLD by 2029; IDE supplies RO technology and operates 20 years, GVPR builds civil works"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbais-11166-crore-desalination-project-advances-as-bmc-seeks-mmb-mpcb-clearances","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-05-10","claim":"Work not begun on ground; MMB and MPCB approvals pending; CRZ clearance obtained end-April"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-bmcs-3500-crore-manori-desalination-project-advances-as-gvpr-engineers-emerge-lowest-bidder","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-10-07","claim":"Estimate raised to Rs 3,500 crore from initial Rs 2,000 crore; tender floated 4 Dec 2023; four failed attempts"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/bmc-defends-200-mld-manori-desalination-plant-amid-environmental-concerns-residents-dispute-consultation-claims","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-11-01","claim":"BMC says it holds CRZ clearance, MPCB consent to establish and MMB NOC; plant still described as proposed"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.213,"lng":72.792},"evidence":"multiple","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"BMCI-13","name":"Manori–Charkop–Mahavir Nagar desalinated water conveyance tunnel","shortName":"Manori water tunnel","summary":"A 7.2 km underground tunnel, running beneath parts of Gorai Creek, to carry desalinated water from the Manori plant to Charkop and on to the existing shaft at Mahavir Nagar, Kandivali. The BMC standing committee cleared the Rs 2,241.3 crore Afcons contract in July 2026, and Afcons announced its letter of acceptance on 6 August 2026. Work was scheduled to begin in August 2026 with a 45-month period, but no report confirms that construction has started. Commissioning is targeted for December 2029.","sector":"Water & sanitation","agency":"BMC","status":"Not started","progress":null,"cost":{"original":null,"revised":2241.3,"note":"Standing committee proposal Rs 2,241.3 crore. Afcons reported its LoA at Rs 1,918 crore including GST and O&M; the figures are not reconciled."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":"Afcons Infrastructure Ltd","startDate":null,"targetDate":"2029-12","revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["Manori","Gorai Creek","Charkop","Mahavir Nagar","Kandivali West"],"constituencies":["Malad West","Charkop"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-bmc-clears-2241-crore-tunnel-project-for-manori-desalination-plant-after-standing-committee-approval","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-07-30","claim":"Standing committee cleared Rs 2,241.3 crore, 7.2 km tunnel for Afcons; 45-month period; commissioning by Dec 2029"},{"url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/in/news-releases/afcons-receives-loa-for-1-918-cr-desalinated-water-tunnel-project-in-mumbai-302844871.html","title":"Afcons Infrastructure press release (PR Newswire / PTI)","date":"2026-08-06","claim":"Afcons received BMC LoA for the Manori-Charkop-Mahavir Nagar desalinated water conveyance tunnel, Rs 1,918 crore including GST and O&M"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.213,"lng":72.792},"evidence":"multiple","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"BMCI-14","name":"New 2,000 MLD water treatment plant at Bhandup Complex","shortName":"Bhandup 2000 MLD WTP","summary":"A new 2,000 MLD water treatment plant on a 7.4-hectare site in the Bhandup Complex. The old 1,910 MLD plant there is not running at full capacity because of structural issues and will be kept running alongside the new one. Welspun Enterprises received the Rs 4,123.88 crore design-build-operate contract in March 2024, with Veolia as technology partner. The 2025-26 BMC budget gave July 2028 for completion. By January 2026 civil, mechanical and electrical works were under way, and completion is now targeted for April 2029.","sector":"Water & sanitation","agency":"BMC","status":"In progress","progress":null,"cost":{"original":null,"revised":4123.88,"note":"Rs 4,123.88 crore LoA value (Mar 2024), including Rs 1,880.44 crore for 15 years of O&M; 48-month build period."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":"Welspun Enterprises Ltd (with Veolia as technology provider)","startDate":null,"targetDate":"2028-07","revisedTargetDate":"2029-04","completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["Bhandup West","Bhandup Complex"],"constituencies":["Bhandup West"],"citywide":true,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-bmc-to-build-new-2000-mld-water-treatment-plant-at-bhandup-by-april-2029","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-01-30","claim":"Work under way; April 2029 completion; 7.4 ha site; replaces 46-year-old plant"},{"url":"https://www.business-standard.com/markets/capital-market-news/welspun-enterprises-wins-contract-of-rs-4123-88-cr-124030100152_1.html","title":"Business Standard","date":"2024-03-01","claim":"Welspun Enterprises received LoA worth Rs 4,123.88 crore from BMC for 2,000 MLD Bhandup WTP"},{"url":"https://theprint.in/economy/welspun-enterprises-gets-rs-4124-crore-order-in-maharashtra/1984716","title":"ThePrint (PTI)","date":"2024-03-01","claim":"Rs 4,123.88 crore including Rs 1,880.44 crore O&M; 48-month build, 15-year O&M"},{"url":"https://www.mcgm.gov.in/irj/go/km/docs/documents/MCGM%20Department%20List/Chief%20Accountant%20(Finance)/Budget/Budget%20Estimate%202025-2026/1-%20MC's%20Speech/BUDGET%20A,B,G/ENGLISH%20SPEECH.pdf","title":"BMC Budget Estimates A, B & G 2025-26 - Municipal Commissioner's budget speech (English)","date":"2025-02-04","claim":"New 2,000 MLD plant at Bhandup; old 1,910 MLD plant (44 years old) not at full capacity due to structural issues; contractor appointed; completion expected July 2028"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.153,"lng":72.944},"evidence":"official","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"BMCI-15","name":"Amar Mahal–Trombay water supply tunnel","shortName":"Amar Mahal–Trombay tunnel","summary":"A 5.5 km TBM-bored water tunnel from Amar Mahal (Hedgewar Udyan, Chembur) to the Trombay high-level reservoir, to improve supply in Chembur, Govandi, Mankhurd and Deonar (M East and M West wards). Excavation and RCC lining were complete by early 2025, and surface pipeline work was due to finish by September 2025. Commissioning then slipped to the end of November 2025. The BMC announced commissioning shutdowns in May 2026, including a 12-hour cut on 18 May. No report found confirms that the tunnel is in regular service.","sector":"Water & sanitation","agency":"BMC","status":"In progress","progress":null,"cost":{"original":null,"revised":null},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":"2025-09","revisedTargetDate":"2025-11","completedDate":null,"delayReason":"Commissioning slipped from September 2025 to end-November 2025 and then to May 2026 commissioning shutdowns; no reason published.","areas":["Chembur","Govandi","Mankhurd","Deonar","Trombay"],"constituencies":["Chembur","Anushakti Nagar","Mankhurd Shivaji Nagar"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-bmc-nears-completion-of-key-water-tunnel-projects-to-boost-supply-across-multiple-wards","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-11-09","claim":"5.5 km tunnel; TBM excavation and lining complete; commissioning moved from Sept 2025 to end-Nov 2025"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-bmc-announces-12-hour-water-cut-in-chembur-govandi-and-mankhurd-on-may-18-for-tunnel-commissioning-work","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-05-15","claim":"12-hour water cut on 18 May 2026 for commissioning of the Amar Mahal (Hedgewar Udyan) tunnel in M East/M West wards"},{"url":"https://www.mcgm.gov.in/irj/go/km/docs/documents/MCGM%20Department%20List/Chief%20Accountant%20(Finance)/Budget/Budget%20Estimate%202025-2026/1-%20MC's%20Speech/BUDGET%20A,B,G/ENGLISH%20SPEECH.pdf","title":"BMC Budget Estimates A, B & G 2025-26 - Municipal Commissioner's budget speech (English)","date":"2025-02-04","claim":"5.50 km Amar Mahal-Trombay HLR tunnel excavation and RCC lining completed; surface pipeline work expected to finish by September 2025; benefits M/East and M/West wards"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.064,"lng":72.901},"evidence":"official","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"BMCI-16","name":"Amar Mahal–Wadala–Parel water supply tunnel","shortName":"Amar Mahal–Parel tunnel","summary":"A 9.7 km water tunnel from Hedgewar Udyan (Amar Mahal) via Pratiksha Nagar (Wadala) to Dhavan Udyan (Parel), to boost supply in Wadala, Sion, Matunga, Parel, Sewri, Byculla and parts of Kurla. The 4.3 km Amar Mahal–Wadala stretch was bored by August 2022. The 5.25 km Wadala–Parel stretch broke through in June 2024. Lining of the Wadala–Parel stretch was still in progress in November 2025, and the work was due by April 2026. The BMC announced a 30-hour shutdown on 5–6 May 2026 to commission the Amar Mahal–Wadala tunnel. No report confirms that either stretch is in regular service.","sector":"Water & sanitation","agency":"BMC","status":"In progress","progress":null,"cost":{"original":null,"revised":null},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":"2026-04","revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["Chembur","Wadala","Sion","Parel","Sewri","Byculla","Kurla"],"constituencies":["Chembur","Sion Koliwada","Wadala","Shivadi"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-bmc-nears-completion-of-key-water-tunnel-projects-to-boost-supply-across-multiple-wards","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-11-09","claim":"9.7 km; excavation complete; Wadala–Parel lining in progress; expected April 2026; wards benefited"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/attention-mumbaikars-bmc-announces-30-hour-water-cut-across-central-eastern-suburbs-on-may-5-6-check-affected-areas","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-05-04","claim":"30-hour shutdown on 5–6 May 2026 to commission the Amar Mahal–Pratiksha Nagar (Wadala) tunnel"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-bmc-completes-525-km-water-tunnel-from-wadala-to-parel-boosting-citys-infrastructure","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2024-06","claim":"5.25 km Wadala–Parel tunnel breakthrough achieved"},{"url":"https://www.mcgm.gov.in/irj/go/km/docs/documents/MCGM%20Department%20List/Chief%20Accountant%20(Finance)/Budget/Budget%20Estimate%202025-2026/1-%20MC's%20Speech/BUDGET%20A,B,G/ENGLISH%20SPEECH.pdf","title":"BMC Budget Estimates A, B & G 2025-26 - Municipal Commissioner's budget speech (English)","date":"2025-02-04","claim":"9.7 km tunnel excavation complete; Amar Mahal-Wadala lining complete, Wadala-Parel in progress; expected to finish by April 2026; benefits F/N, F/S and parts of E and L wards"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.064,"lng":72.901},"evidence":"official","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"BMCI-17","name":"Yewai–Kasheli–Mulund water conveyance tunnel","shortName":"Yewai–Mulund tunnel","summary":"A 21 km deep water tunnel in two sections, bringing Bhatsa-system water from the Yewai master balancing reservoir via Kasheli (Bhiwandi) to Mulund Octroi Naka. It will allow realignment of the Mumbai I and II surface mains in Thane. A work order has been issued for the 14 km Yewai–Kasheli section. The work order for the 7.13 km Kasheli–Mulund section was issued in September 2024, and Afcons is building it. In July 2026 the 134 m Mulund launch shaft was complete and TBM boring was due to start by September 2026. The Kasheli–Mulund section is targeted for October 2030.","sector":"Water & sanitation","agency":"BMC","status":"In progress","progress":null,"cost":{"original":4500,"revised":null,"note":"About Rs 4,500 crore for the full 21 km (FPJ, Sept 2024); section-wise contract values not verified in an approved source."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":"Afcons Infrastructure Ltd (Kasheli–Mulund section); Yewai–Kasheli contractor not verified in an approved source","startDate":"2024-09","targetDate":"2030-10","revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["Mulund","Mulund Octroi Naka","Kasheli (Bhiwandi, outside Mumbai)","Yewai (outside Mumbai)"],"constituencies":["Mulund"],"citywide":true,"sources":[{"url":"https://freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-infra-update-bmc-to-begin-tbm-work-on-kasheli-mulund-water-tunnel-by-september-713-km-project-targeted-for-2030-completion","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-07-22","claim":"Kasheli–Mulund 7.13 km; TBM boring to start by September 2026; Mulund shaft complete; target October 2030; construction began September 2024"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/amp/mumbai/bmc-begins-work-on-21-km-thane-mulund-water-tunnel","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2024-09-19","claim":"21 km (14 km Yewai–Kasheli + 7 km Kasheli–Mulund), about Rs 4,500 crore; work order issued"},{"url":"https://www.mcgm.gov.in/irj/go/km/docs/documents/MCGM%20Department%20List/Chief%20Accountant%20(Finance)/Budget/Budget%20Estimate%202025-2026/1-%20MC's%20Speech/BUDGET%20A,B,G/ENGLISH%20SPEECH.pdf","title":"BMC Budget Estimates A, B & G 2025-26 - Municipal Commissioner's budget speech (English)","date":"2025-02-04","claim":"Kasheli-Mulund tunnel work order issued September 2024, completion expected October 2030; Yewai-Kasheli tunnel work order issued and preliminary work in progress"},{"url":"https://m.thewire.in/article/ptiprnews/afcons-receives-loa-for-%E2%82%B91918-cr-desalinated-water-tunnel-project-in-mumbai","title":"The Wire (PTI press-release feed, Afcons)","date":"2026-08-06","claim":"Afcons is executing BMC's 7.13 km Kasheli-Mulund underground water conveyance tunnel"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.242,"lng":73.015},"evidence":"official","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"BMCI-18","name":"Mahalaxmi Racecourse 'Mumbai Central Park' and underground facilities","shortName":"Racecourse Central Park","summary":"A BMC plan, announced in December 2025 and presented in February 2026, to combine about 120–125 acres of the Mahalaxmi racecourse with about 170 acres of Coastal Road reclaimed land as a 'Central Park'. It includes gardens, an underground sports arena, a convention centre, three basement car parks (parking for about 5,000 vehicles, per the December announcement) and a subway to the Coastal Road. The subway tender had been issued by February 2026, and in August 2026 the standing committee approved a Rs 702.44 crore underground pedestrian link to be built by MMRCL. The basements were at the feasibility stage. Groups of architects objected over flood risk, transparency and lease terms. Construction of the park itself has not started.","sector":"Heritage & public spaces","agency":"BMC","status":"Not started","progress":0,"cost":{"original":null,"revised":null,"note":"Subway about Rs 500 crore (commissioner, Feb 2026). In Aug 2026 the standing committee approved a Rs 702.44 crore, 1.518 km underground pedestrian link from the Science Centre Metro station / racecourse area to the Coastal Road promenade, to be executed by MMRCL. No estimate published for the basements or the park."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":"Feasibility study for the basements pending; objections from the Mumbai Architects Collective over flood risk, transparency and lease terms","areas":["Mahalaxmi","Mahalaxmi Racecourse","Haji Ali","Coastal Road"],"constituencies":["Worli"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/bmc-unveils-mahalaxmi-racecourse-central-park-plan-amid-mac-objections","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-02-22","claim":"Master plan components; three basement parkings under feasibility study; subway tendered at about Rs 500 crore; MAC objections"},{"url":"https://swarajyamag.com/amp/story/news-brief/mumbai-architects-warn-6200-parking-bays-could-harm-flood-resilience-at-mahalaxmi-racecourse","title":"Swarajya","date":null,"claim":"Architects warn about 5,000 new underground parking bays could harm flood resilience"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-bmc-approves-70244-crore-underground-pedestrian-link-from-mahalaxmi-to-coastal-road-despite-opposition","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-08-20","claim":"Standing committee approved Rs 702.44 crore, 1.518 km underground pedestrian passage from Science Centre Metro/Mahalaxmi Racecourse area to Coastal Road promenade; MMRCL to execute"},{"url":"https://www.mcgm.gov.in/irj/go/km/docs/documents/MCGM%20Department%20List/Chief%20Accountant%20(Finance)/Budget/Budget%20Estimate%202025-2026/1-%20MC's%20Speech/BUDGET%20A,B,G/ENGLISH%20SPEECH.pdf","title":"BMC Budget Estimates A, B & G 2025-26 - Municipal Commissioner's budget speech (English)","date":"2025-02-04","claim":"'Mumbai Public Park' planned on 120.12 acres of racecourse land plus 170 acres of Coastal Road reclaimed land; consultant appointed for racecourse design; EOI invited for 170 acres"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":18.9825,"lng":72.818},"evidence":"official","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"}
